Prealgebra 2e — Marecek, Anthony-Smith, and Mathis (@ql-source-prealgebra: 0, is #book, #part-of @ql-sources) { r_36KCS76R5ZTWZMVPV5B11Y3BKS
Lynn Marecek, MaryAnne Anthony-Smith, and Andrea Honeycutt Mathis. Prealgebra 2e. OpenStax, Rice University, 2020. English.

[Book and PDF access](https://openstax.org/details/books/prealgebra-2e) · [Preface and scope](https://openstax.org/books/prealgebra-2e/pages/preface).

This is the extended arithmetic-to-algebra reading. Complete chapters 1–11 for the fullest foundation, using the chapter reviews and practice tests. In particular, return to chapter 3 for integers, 7 for real-number properties and measurement, 8 for linear equations, 9 for geometric models, 10 for exponents and scientific notation, and 11 for graphs. The trail's shorter trade books and this text are complementary choices; they are not successive copies of the same compulsory exercise set.

The current publisher web edition states CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and includes separate reuse notices. Some earlier distributed editions carry different notices; inspect the actual edition before copying or adapting it. Free reading and linking do not require assuming unrestricted redistribution. Preserve the authors, edition, source, and component credits. No textbook text or PDF is reproduced in the repository. Publisher preface, chapter outline, and current notice checked on 28 October 2026.

